 "decision": "Keep the original RIFE v4.26. Every attempt raised PSNR (up to +0.39 dB) but LPIPS got worse (best 0.0473 vs 0.0457), already by the first eval and even at LR 2e-6, so fine-tuning on three films trades sharpness of the middle frame for average-pixel accuracy. Next ideas: much more and more varied real-motion data, distillation against the original model as teacher, or only fine-tuning the last IFBlock."
